            0.108
          ],
          "content": "WS 2021-22"
        },
        {
          "type": "header",
          "bbox": [
            0.817,
            0.093,
            0.9,
            0.107
          ],
          "content": "Seite 234"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.131,
            0.133,
            0.89,
            0.15
          ],
          "content": "Nun bleibt noch zu zeigen, dass  $P^{2}=P$  ist. Dazu sei  $v\\in V$ . Wir wenden P zweimal an:"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.182,
            0.161,
            0.841,
            0.24
          ],
          "content": "\\begin{array}{l} \\left(P ^ {2} v\\right) (x) = \\left(P (P v)\\right) (x) = P \\left(\\frac {v (x) + v (- x)}{2}\\right) = \\frac {\\frac {v (x) + v (- x)}{2} + \\frac {v (- x) + v (- (- x))}{2}}{2} \\\\ = \\frac {v (x) + v (- x)}{2} = (P v) (x). \\\\ \\end{array}",
          "image_source": "../../raw/pages_0225-0240/images/page_239_equation_4.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.132,
            0.249,
            0.525,
            0.267
          ],
          "content": "Damit ist gezeigt, dass P eine Projektion ist."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.292,
            0.519,
            0.312
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "B.5.3 Lineare Gleichungssysteme"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.135,
            0.327,
            0.48,
            0.349
          ],
          "content": "Teillösung zur Übung 8.4.6. Bild( $\\underline{A}$ ) ist"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.405,
            0.359,
            0.614,
            0.417
          ],
          "content": "\\mathrm{Sp} \\left\\{\\left( \\begin{array}{c} 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ - 1 \\end{array} \\right), \\left( \\begin{array}{c} 0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ - 1 \\end{array} \\right) \\right\\}.",
          "image_source": "../../raw/pages_0225-0240/images/page_239_equation_8.jpg"
        },
